// Jahshaka's SKY CAPTURE (SKY-GPU, 2026-09-13).
//
// Six render_scene passes over RENDER QUEUE 0 ALONE — the queue every sky
// renderable in this engine sits in (OgreSky.cpp's tuneSkyRenderable moves
// Ogre's own sky quad there, and the analytic sky's quad with it) — into the
// six faces of a small cubemap, with `camera_cubemap_reorient` turning one
// camera into the six face directions.
//
// WHAT IT REPLACES: the host used to resample its equirect sky image into six
// 128^2 faces on the CPU (6 x 16k bilinear fetches per sky change, on the UI
// thread) and integrate the sky's ambient over the whole image. Now the sky is
// captured from the very shader the viewport draws it with, so a photograph, a
// baked gradient strip, a picked colour and the analytic sky all reach the
// reflections and the ambient through one path. The capture is the input of
// the ibl_specular convolution (JahshakaIbl.compositor) and of the SH integral
// (OgreSky.cpp, from the 32^2 mip).
//
// visibility_mask 0x1 is kVisibleBit: the sun disc carries kSunDiscBit INSTEAD
// (EnginePrivate.h), so it is never captured into the environment — the disc is
// drawn, the sun's energy is the directional light's.
//
// THE QUEUE RANGE, AND THE ONE MEASUREMENT THAT DECIDED IT. `rq_last` is
// documented as exclusive (our own PCC compositor says so) — but with this pass
// at `0 1` the SUN DISC, which sits at render queue 1, landed in the capture the
// moment `world.sunDisc({inProbes:true})` gave it kVisibleBit: the scene's
// ambient went from 0.117 to 1.01 at a HALF-DEGREE disc and to 4.30 at 170
// degrees. Setting `rq_last 0` then captured nothing at all, which says the
// range really is exclusive and the leak is somewhere else in the cull.
//
// So the disc is kept out by the only means that is not in question: it lives
// at render queue 5 now (OgreSky.cpp's applySunDisc), which no capture pass in
// this engine asks for. The sun's energy reaches surfaces through the
// DIRECTIONAL LIGHT; a disc in the 9-band integral would be that light twice,
// and the disc's size is a dial that goes to 10 degrees.
//
// A scene render with no geometry in range still walks the cull, which is why
// this runs on a sky CHANGE and never per frame.
//
// external 0 = the capture cube (RenderToTexture + AllowAutomipmaps)

abstract target jah_sky_face
{
	pass render_scene
	{
		load
		{
			all				clear
			clear_colour	0 0 0 1
		}
		store
		{
			depth			dont_care
			stencil			dont_care
		}

		rq_first			0
		rq_last				1
		visibility_mask		0x1
		overlays			off
		camera_cubemap_reorient true

		profiling_id "Jahshaka sky capture"
	}
}

compositor_node JahshakaSkyCaptureNode
{
	in 0 skyCapture

	target skyCapture +X : jah_sky_face { }
	target skyCapture -X : jah_sky_face { }
	target skyCapture +Y : jah_sky_face { }
	target skyCapture -Y : jah_sky_face { }
	target skyCapture +Z : jah_sky_face { }
	target skyCapture -Z : jah_sky_face { }
}

workspace JahshakaSkyCaptureWorkspace
{
	connect_external 0 JahshakaSkyCaptureNode 0
}
